<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH OKD TAKES 35 PCT STAKE IN TEP KARVINA-CTK.</title>
<headline>CZECH OKD TAKES 35 PCT STAKE IN TEP KARVINA-CTK.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech coal miner OKD a.s. has taken a 34.7 percent stake in heating utility Teplarny Karvina a.s., the CTK nes agency reported on Friday.</p>
<p>CTK quoted OKD General Director Ivan Dzida as saying the transaction occurred on Tuesday. He gave no further details.</p>
<p>Officials of both companies were not available immediately for comment.</p>
<p>OKD, located in the Moravian city of Ostrava, is the country's largest coal miner.</p>
<p>It recently took a majority stake in another heating utility, Moravskoslezske Teplarny a.s., in tandem with the local firm Prosper trading.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
